# p10-preview.ps1 - builds the app and serves it on localhost for the owner's visual check (P10 T11q: the NEW Admin window from the two mock-ups, plus the Colour theme).
# Same server as p05..p09-preview: pinned to localhost:4173 (the owner is already registered there; otherwise Register first).
# This script keeps running (the server). Stop it with Ctrl+C.
# Run (NOT through run.cmd, because it never finishes):
#   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\scripts\p10-preview.ps1"
# For the phone: keep THIS window running, open a SECOND PowerShell window and run:
#   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\scripts\p04-phone.ps1"
# It prints an https link; open that link on the phone and add  #/admin  at the end (the phone has its own data, so Register there first).
# The GitHub token is typed ONLY into the Admin page. Never paste it into the chat with Claude.

npm run build
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host "Build failed." -ForegroundColor Red; exit 1 }

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "Open in a NORMAL Chrome window (not Incognito):  http://localhost:4173/   (Admin page: http://localhost:4173/#/admin)" -ForegroundColor Green
Write-Host "If the page behaves like the OLD version after a new build: close EVERY tab of localhost:4173 and open it again, or F12 > Application > Service Workers > Unregister, then Ctrl+Shift+R. Do NOT use 'Clear site data' (it deletes your registration)." -ForegroundColor Yellow
Write-Host "Walk-through (P10 Admin, the NEW window from your two mock-ups). P10 only READS from GitHub (token check, load published courses): nothing is written online and Publish / Unpublish are OFF (that is P11). Texts in the window are English; only the three box hints are Gujarati." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "KNOWN, not a bug (tell me if you want any of them changed): (a) a NEW course gets its name in the Settings (gear) panel; (b) letter boxes (circle, square ...) are not drawn inside the editing box while you type; (c) Bold / Italic need SELECTED text, typing after pressing Bold on an empty cursor does not work yet; (d) Ctrl+V pastes PLAIN text, Word formatting is not kept; (e) the user app shows the new styles only after Publish (P11), today this window is the check; (f) the Test part is still the old paste box (a Generate test button replaces it later)." -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "  1. HIDDEN: on Home and in the bottom bar / menu there is NO Admin tile and NO Admin link. Only the address ending with #/admin opens it." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  2. LOGIN: open #/admin. Type a wrong text (for example abc) and press Log in: a friendly message, no raw error. Then paste your REAL GitHub token (github_pat_...) and press Log in: you see 'signed in'. The token is not shown anywhere afterwards. Press Log out: the form comes back EMPTY. Log in again." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  3. COURSE LIST: after login the Add button (add a course) is at the very TOP and all your courses are below it, each with Edit, Delete, Publish and Unpublish. Publish and Unpublish are OFF with a note. Press Delete: a question appears (Yes, delete / No, keep it); Yes marks the course 'Marked as deleted', Restore brings it back. Press 'Load a published course' and Load one: it opens as a draft that is NOT saved until you press Save." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  4. THE NEW WINDOW: press the Add button and compare with your mock-ups: a toolbar of 6 colourful buttons (Fonts, Style, Box styles, Colour, Add picture, Settings; 3 + 3 on a narrow window, one row when wide), ONE white window with three dashed boxes (Title yellow and optional, Subtitle blue, Content purple and big) with the Gujarati hints, a bottom bar Save / Edit chapters / Publish, and Add chapter under it. Press Settings (the gear): Course title, Short description, Order, Choose cover. Press Save with the course title EMPTY first: a list of problems, nothing saved. Then give a Gujarati course title and an order number (and a cover if you like)." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  5. WRITE: type a Gujarati Title (or leave it empty), a Subtitle and a long Content paragraph with several lines (Enter = a new line). Paste some text with Ctrl+V: it arrives as plain text. In the Style panel press Bullet list with the cursor on a line: the line gets a bullet; press it again: the bullet goes." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  6. FONTS: select some words and open Fonts: three groups (Gujarati fonts, Hindi and Sanskrit, English) and a Default font button. Press a few fonts: the selected words change shape at once. Try all 16 if you like (Kumar One is a display font: good for titles, tiring in long text). On a narrow window the panel must stay easy to use: tell me if the 16 fonts feel crowded." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  7. STYLE + SIZE: select words and press Bold, Italic, Underline and Highlight (with nothing selected you get a hint), then Clear style. Choose Smaller, Normal size, Large, Extra large and Biggest: the size changes each time." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  8. BOX STYLES: select a few letters and choose a Letter box (circle, square, diamond, rounded square; light or dark). Select a word and choose a Word box (box, pill, dashed, double line, underline bar). Put the cursor in a line and choose a Paragraph box (box, rounded, dashed, double line, left bar, shadow). The Remove buttons take them away again." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "  9. COLOUR: give a letter, a word and a whole line a text colour (Red, Orange, Brown, Green, Teal, Blue, Purple, Pink). No colour removes it. Look at the same text again in step 15 (Light, Dark, Colour): every colour must stay readable." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 10. PICTURE AT THE CURSOR: click in the MIDDLE of the paragraph and press Add picture, choose a photo: the text splits into two boxes with the picture card between them (a big photo is made smaller with a short message). Describe the picture in its box, or leave the box empty (that is allowed). Put the cursor in the Title or Subtitle box and add a picture: it goes to the TOP of the content. Remove picture takes it out." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 11. PICTURE SIZE + POSITION: on the picture card drag a side edge (width), drag the bottom edge (height), slide the picture left or right. The buttons do the same: Narrower / Wider / Shorter / Taller and Left / Centre / Right, and the width and height boxes take numbers. On the phone put a finger ON the picture and try to scroll the page: tell me if it feels stuck (the picture holds the finger on purpose, so it can slide)." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 12. CHAPTERS: press Add chapter: a NEW chapter window opens after the current one; write a Title and one paragraph. Press Edit chapters: the chapter list shows both. Open one, Down moves it, Up brings it back, Delete asks 'Delete ... and everything in it?': press 'No, keep it'. Switch the parts Overview | Content | Test and back: your text is still there." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 13. TEST PART: open the part Test and paste these lines (the correct answer has ** on both sides):" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "        1. What is 2 + 2?" -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "        3" -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "        **4**" -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "        5" -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "        6" -ForegroundColor Gray
Write-Host "     One question appears. Paste the same lines again WITHOUT the stars: a message with the line number says which option must be bold. Set 'Questions per game' to 1 and to a wrong value like abc (a friendly message)." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 14. SAVE + KEPT + PUBLISH: press Save: 'The course was saved in this browser.' appears. Reload the page (F5), open #/admin, log in, press Edit on the course: the SAME text, fonts, sizes, colours, boxes, pictures with their size and position, chapters in the same order, the cover and the test are all back. The Publish button in the window is OFF and the note says 'Publishing comes in the next phase. For now, Save keeps the course as a draft in this browser.'" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 15. THEMES + KEYBOARD (PC): in the app Settings choose Light, then Dark, then Colour (the new pastel theme; System is gone, an old saved System lands on Light). In EACH theme look at Home, a course, the Admin list, the window with its toolbar and the Settings page: texts, buttons, tiles, cards and the bottom bar must be readable; in Colour every pastel tile / card has DARK text of the same colour, also secondary buttons and text boxes on a pastel card. (The Admin cards and the toolbar buttons keep the page colours on purpose: tell me if you want them pastel too.) Then Tab through the window: every control has a visible focus ring and the order feels natural." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host " 16. NARROW + PHONE: make the window narrow (about 360 px; Chrome: F12, then Ctrl+Shift+M): no sideways scroll, nothing overlaps, the toolbar shows 3 + 3 buttons, long Gujarati titles wrap, the bottom bar buttons are easy to hit. Then on the phone (link from p04-phone.ps1 + #/admin): log in, add a course with one chapter, one picture and one coloured word, Save, Edit: everything readable and tappable, also in the Colour theme." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "Tell Claude (in Gujarati is fine) what looks wrong, or say 'all good'. NEVER send the token." -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "Stop the server with Ctrl+C." -ForegroundColor Yellow
npm run preview -- --host localhost --port 4173 --strictPort
